# Pass-1 OCR uses the same OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint as the AI agents
# (LiteLLM proxying dots.ocr). Configure via admin settings, NOT env:
#   ai_base_url   — LiteLLM base URL (…/v1)
#   ai_api_key    — LiteLLM key
#   ai_model.ocr  — the dots.ocr model id LiteLLM routes to
# Born-digital PDFs are text-extracted in-process (pdf-parse); scanned PDFs are
# rasterised with poppler (pdftoppm) before OCR. No OCR sidecar to run.

# === Email intake (mailbox connectors) ===
# Unlike the AI settings above, this IS an env var. 32-byte hex key that encrypts
# stored mailbox credentials (IMAP passwords / OAuth refresh tokens) at rest.
# Required to add any mailbox connector; without it the API 500s on connect.
# Generate once and keep it stable (rotation invalidates all stored credentials):
#   export MAILBOX_SECRET_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
MAILBOX_SECRET_KEY=
